B.bF=new A.mN(0,"log")
B.U9=new A.c1(B.bF,"FROM THE DESK DRAWER \u2014 LOG OF R. HALLORAN, NIGHT OPERATOR","Whoever is reading this: the rundown is a lie and the quotas are real. Keep the needle up. It does not care what you broadcast, only that you are broadcasting.",null)
B.U1=new A.c1(B.bZ,"KBLK-7 \u2014 TO ALL OVERNIGHT STAFF \u2014 11 MARCH 1971","The transmitter is not to be taken off air for maintenance, weather, power supply, industrial action, or any other reason. Maintenance is to be carried out live. If this is not possible, it is to be carried out anyway.","H. BRENNAN, STATION MANAGER")
B.TU=new A.c1(B.bF,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 214","Eight of them. There have only ever been eight. I have a key for each and I have never needed a ninth, which I used to find comforting.",null)
B.e_=new A.mN(3,"engineering")
B.U2=new A.c1(B.e_,"MERIDIAN CATHODE LTD \u2014 INSTALLATION NOTE, MODEL 7","The set in booth two is not a monitor. It is the aerial. Anything that appears on it is already inside the building, and the picture is the last place you will see it before the room is.","FITTED 1963. DO NOT REPLACE.")
B.iS=new A.mN(2,"letter")
B.U7=new A.c1(B.iS,"LETTER \u2014 POSTMARKED 2 OCTOBER 1974","Dear Sir, my husband sat up with your station on Tuesday night as he cannot sleep. He says a man on the test card said his name and the name of our road. He will not go in that room now. We do not want an apology. We want to know how you knew.",null)
B.TS=new A.c1(B.bF,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 341","They have started arriving in the order I think of them in. I have stopped keeping the list in order.",null)
B.TZ=new A.c1(B.bZ,"KBLK-7 \u2014 OPERATOR ROSTER, REVISED \u2014 4 JANUARY 1976","The overnight shift is a one-man post and will remain a one-man post. Requests for a second operator have been declined on the grounds that a second operator has, historically, not survived the arrangement any better than the first.","H. BRENNAN")
B.TN=new A.c1(B.bF,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 508","The window in the booth does not open and has never opened. Whatever is in the field is not getting in that way. I want to be clear that this is the only reassuring sentence in this book.",null)
B.iT=new A.mN(4,"transcript")
B.U_=new A.c1(B.iT,"OFF-AIR RECORDING \u2014 03:14, 19 JUNE 1977 \u2014 UNSCHEDULED",'[TONE, 1000Hz, 41 SECONDS]\n"...and that is the end of the programmes for tonight. We close down now. We close down now. We close down now. We close down now. We do not close down. Goodnight."',null)
B.TP=new A.c1(B.e_,"CARRIER NOTE \u2014 UNSIGNED, PENCIL, ON THE BACK OF A SCHEDULE","Asked Brennan what happens if it drops. He said it has never dropped. I said that is not what I asked. He said it has never dropped, and wrote it down, as if writing it down was the job.",null)
B.U6=new A.c1(B.bF,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 720","Slept four hours in the chair with the carrier up. Woke to find the log open at a page I had not written yet. The handwriting is mine.",null)
B.U0=new A.c1(B.iS,"LETTER \u2014 POSTMARKED 30 NOVEMBER 1979","I am eleven. I am not supposed to be up. There was a lady on your channel standing very still in front of the colour bars and she was not on the colour bars, she was in front of them, and the bars went behind her properly like she was in the room where you make it. I waved. She waved back after a bit.",null)
B.TX=new A.c1(B.bZ,"KBLK-7 \u2014 NOTICE TO ENGINEERING \u2014 8 AUGUST 1981","The pen recorder in booth two is to be inked at the start of every shift without exception. The trace is not a formality. If the trace stops, the operator is to assume the trace is correct and that he is the thing that has stopped.",null)
B.U8=new A.c1(B.bF,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 901","It is not trying to get out. I have had this backwards for two years. It is trying to get me to stop, which is a different thing, and it is much more patient about it.",null)
B.U3=new A.c1(B.e_,"MAST LOG \u2014 CLIMB REPORT, 12 FEBRUARY 1982","Went up to change the beacon. There are handholds worn into the ladder above the two hundred foot mark, on the inside face, where nobody climbing would put their hands. They are worn deep. Whatever made them has been going up and down that mast for a very long time and it does not use the rungs.",null)
B.TK=new A.c1(B.iT,"OFF-AIR RECORDING \u2014 04:02, 3 MAY 1983 \u2014 UNSCHEDULED",'[NO VIDEO. AUDIO ONLY.]\n"Is he still there."\n"He is still there."\n"He has been there a long time."\n"He will not be there a long time."\n[TONE RESUMES]',null)
B.TV=new A.c1(B.bZ,"KBLK-7 \u2014 FROM THE OFFICE OF H. BRENNAN \u2014 1 DECEMBER 1984","To the night operator. You will have noticed that nobody thanks you and that the day staff do not meet your eye. This is not unkindness. They have read the file and you have not, and they have decided that the difference is the only thing keeping you at that desk. I am inclined to agree with them.",null)
B.TO=new A.c1(B.bF,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 1,114","There is a second operator on the roster now. I have not met them. I have not been told their name. The roster is in my handwriting.",null)
B.TQ=new A.c1(B.bF,"HALLORAN \u2014 FINAL ENTRY","If you are new: it is not the noise. It is the quiet after the noise, when you have got it right and you are sitting there being pleased with yourself. That is when it looks at you properly.",null)
B.TY=new A.c1(B.bZ,"STATION MEMO \u2014 UNSIGNED, UNDATED","R. HALLORAN did not sign off on the morning of the 1,115th night. The carrier was up. The chair was warm. The log was open to a blank page, and the page is the one you have been writing on.",null)
B.TL=new A.c1(B.e_,"FCC \u2014 NOTICE OF LICENCE REVOCATION \u2014 14 JULY 1987","Authority to broadcast on 1,140 kHz is withdrawn effective immediately. All transmission is to cease. Confirmation of shutdown is required in writing within seven days.","NO CONFIRMATION WAS EVER RECEIVED.")
B.TM=new A.c1(B.bZ,"KBLK-7 \u2014 INTERNAL, 15 JULY 1987","We are not going to comply and we are not going to explain why we are not going to comply, because the explanation is worse than the fine. Keep the carrier up. Pay whatever they ask.","H. BRENNAN")
B.TW=new A.c1(B.iS,"LETTER \u2014 POSTMARKED 2 AUGUST 1987","You are still on. I checked. My set has been in the loft since my wife passed and I got it down because I could hear it through the ceiling. It is not plugged in. I would like someone to come and take it away and I would like them to come in the daytime.",null)
B.U4=new A.c1(B.iT,"OFF-AIR RECORDING \u2014 05:51, DATE ILLEGIBLE",'"How long has he been on the roster."\n"Since the beginning."\n"He does not think he has been."\n"He never does. That is what makes him good at it."',null)
B.TT=new A.c1(B.e_,"MERIDIAN CATHODE LTD \u2014 SERVICE BULLETIN, MODEL 7","Owners of the Model 7 are advised that the set has no off switch by design and that the absence is not a fault. Attempts to fit one have been made by three separate engineers. Their reports are consistent and are not reproduced here.",null)
B.TR=new A.c1(B.bZ,"KBLK-7 \u2014 PAYROLL, ANNOTATED IN PENCIL","Night operator, one post, continuous since 1963. Twenty-two names in twenty-four years. Nineteen resignations, none of them written. Two retirements, neither of them attended. One still on shift.",null)
B.U5=new A.c1(B.bF,"A PAGE IN YOUR OWN HANDWRITING THAT YOU DO NOT REMEMBER WRITING","Keep the needle up. It does not care what you broadcast, only that you are broadcasting. Whoever is reading this: the rundown is a lie and the quotas are real.","THE DATE ON IT IS TONIGHT.")
B.jN=s([B.U9,B.U1,B.TU,B.U2,B.U7,B.TS,B.TZ,B.TN,B.U_,B.TP,B.U6,B.U0,B.TX,B.U8,B.U3,B.TK,B.TV,B.TO,B.TQ,B.TY,B.TL,B.TM,B.TW,B.U4,B.TT,B.TR,B.U5],t.v2)
B.PU=new A.ch("D. KEEL",1,"PROBATIONARY","Did not come back for a second shift. Left the badge on the desk.","THE CANTEEN opens.")
B.Q_=new A.ch("M. ARDEN",2,"NIGHT OPERATOR","Resigned by telephone, at 06:04, from a call box outside.","THE FILE \u2014 one document recovered from the desk every night.")
B.PI=new A.ch("S. BRIGHT",4,"OPERATOR, SECOND CLASS","Transferred to daytime. Would not say why in writing.","THE STATION BOARD \u2014 permanent upgrades bought with RATINGS POINTS.")
B.PN=new A.ch("R. OKONKWO",7,"OPERATOR, FIRST CLASS","Took the annual leave he was owed and did not use the return half.","THE TOOL RACK \u2014 charged equipment on the Q-T row.")
B.PQ=new A.ch("J. FENN",11,"SENIOR OPERATOR","Signed off every morning for eleven days and then simply did not sign on.","AUTOMATION \u2014 the bots on the AUTO tab.")
B.PL=new A.ch("A. VOSS",16,"DUTY OPERATOR","Requested a second operator in writing four times. Filed the refusals in date order.","A ninth key. It is not on the deck yet.")
B.PZ=new A.ch("P. LARSSON",23,"SHIFT SUPERVISOR","Kept a tally on the underside of the desk. It stops at 23.",null)
B.PR=new A.ch("E. MARSH",32,"DUTY SUPERVISOR",'Wrote "IT IS NOT THE NOISE" on the wall behind the rack. It is still there.',null)
B.PK=new A.ch("C. IVERS",45,"TRANSMISSION CONTROLLER","Stopped using the corridor. Slept in the booth for the last three weeks of it.",null)
B.PS=new A.ch("B. NAKASHIMA",62,"SENIOR CONTROLLER","Asked the day staff to stop leaving him notes. They had not been leaving him notes.",null)
B.PJ=new A.ch("T. GRUBER",84,"CHIEF OPERATOR","Logged every hour of every shift. The last forty entries are in someone else's hand.",null)
B.PP=new A.ch("W. ODELL",112,"DUTY ENGINEER","Climbed the mast once. Would not say what the handholds were.",null)
B.PG=new A.ch("N. PRYCE",150,"SENIOR ENGINEER","Requested the booth window be bricked up. The request was approved and never carried out.",null)
B.PY=new A.ch("F. AMANI",200,"TRANSMISSION ENGINEER","Two hundred nights without a single missed quota. No note, no resignation, no last shift.",null)
B.PF=new A.ch("K. SOLT",268,"STATION ENGINEER","Started signing the book with the previous operator's name. Nobody corrected him.",null)
B.PO=new A.ch("H. VANCE",355,"DUTY MANAGER","The only one who ever turned the carrier down. For nine seconds.",null)
B.PV=new A.ch("G. REEDY",470,"NIGHT MANAGER","Left a full flask and a coat on the back of the chair. Both are still there.",null)
B.PM=new A.ch("L. ASHE",620,"SENIOR NIGHT MANAGER","Stopped appearing in the day staff's accounts of the handover, while continuing to attend it.",null)
B.PT=new A.ch("V. CORRIGAN",810,"CONTROLLER OF TRANSMISSION","Answered the phone in the booth. There is no phone in the booth.",null)
B.PX=new A.ch("O. STRAND",1000,"DEPUTY CHIEF","A thousand nights. The card in the vault has his face on it.",null)
B.PH=new A.ch("I. BRENNAN",1080,"CHIEF OF TRANSMISSION","Wrote the memos. Signed the refusals. Sat the post himself for the last eleven weeks of it.",null)
B.PW=new A.ch("R. HALLORAN",1114,"THE LONGEST NIGHT","Did not sign off on the morning of the 1,115th. The carrier was up. The chair was warm.","There is nobody left on the roster above you.")
B.d3=s([B.PU,B.Q_,B.PI,B.PN,B.PQ,B.PL,B.PZ,B.PR,B.PK,B.PS,B.PJ,B.PP,B.PG,B.PY,B.PF,B.PO,B.PV,B.PM,B.PT,B.PX,B.PH,B.PW],A.a8("r<ch>"))
